     "idx": 31,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p131",
     "text": "Constructing a Dyson sphere represents a civilization\u2019s triumphant ascension from planetary fragility to cosmic immortality, fundamentally reshaping their destiny across an artificial firmament. By harnessing the totality of their captive star, these cosmic architects extinguish scarcity forever, tr"
    },
    {
     "idx": 35,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p008",
     "text": "Across the velvet abyss, ascending civilizations transcend the humble cradle of their birth to claim the architecture of the cosmos. First arise the planetary masters, who tame seismic tempests and orchestrate their homeworld's volcanic fury into a unified pulse of clean planetary power. Yet their a"
    },
    {
     "idx": 81,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p046",
     "text": "For fifteen centuries, Egypt lay locked in profound silence, its monumental hieroglyphs reduced to mute, decorative riddles. Then, in 1822, Champollion finally cracked the Rosetta Stone\u2019s trilingual code. Instantly, the ancient darkness broke. Pharaohs, priests, and forgotten scribes began to speak "
    },
    {
     "idx": 100,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p077",
     "text": "Suppose the heavens are merely painted linen and the floor beneath your soles a tapestry woven by an industrious fiend. To gaze into the world under such an unsettling suspicion is to suffer a sudden, sickening vertigo, as if every solid masonry of reality had dissolved into thin air. Flesh becomes "
    },
    {
     "idx": 213,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p016",
     "text": "Across the vast, silent expanse of the cosmos, the brilliant tapestry of shining stars, glowing nebulae, and whirling galaxies represents merely the illuminated trim of an unfathomably grander, hidden architecture. Pervading the void lies dark matter, acting as an invisible scaffolding that firmly u"
    },
    {
     "idx": 217,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p028",
     "text": "Pulled from the sunless Aegean abyss among shattered amphorae and barnacled marble, the lump of encrusted verdigris resembled nothing more than an unremarkable stone. Yet beneath centuries of petrified marine sediment lay antiquity\u2019s most astonishing secret: a bronze cosmos frozen in corrosion. Meti"
    },
    {
     "idx": 219,
     "prompt_group": "tr:p083",
     "text": "Bound by atomic clocks and collective wonder, humanity stitched scattered observatories across continents into a single planetary eye. From frozen polar ice to high desert plateaus, distant radio dishes breathed in unison, transforming our spinning globe into a colossal virtual lens. Together, these"
    },
    {
     "idx": 242,
